    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136">

                <pb facs="0133" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">745.93/10–1249: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-12T16:00:00+01:00">October 12, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 12—12:22 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4092. Indian High Commissioner informed American correspondent in confidence
                    October 10 Nehru had (1) recalled Indian Ambassador China, (2) exchanged cordial
                    messages with Mme. Sun Yatsen<anchor n="19" xml:id="d136-f1"/> and (3) sent
                    favorable and friendly reply Communist Foreign Minister re establishment Central
                    People’s Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d136-f1" n="19" xml:id="d136-f1-content">
                <p>Member of Communist-sponsored Chinese People’s Political Consultative Conference
                    and a Vice Chairman of the “Central Government of the People’s Republic of
                    China”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
